# World 2's chip budget (SPEC 11, "World 2, slice 2"): the DPS logo of the boot splash (37,456 bytes and its two
# copper lists, 47 KB) is freed at the title, right after the splash (v1.40: `AGK splash freed`; the first version of this
# test saw it freed when world 2 loaded, which is the same memory at the same point of the game). Slice 2's BOBs are in two blocks: the common set (radar, windsock, rope, hook, climbing man:
# 7,968 bytes) from the world's load, and the mission's own part (mission 5: the ship deck, 5,760; mission 6: the freighter and the strait
# destroyer's set, 25,616) made at the mission's card and freed at the next one (the per-mission lever, v1.24). The game prints the chip
# free to the byte after each: a500 measured 139,416 in mission 4 (136 KB), 133,656 in mission 5 (130), 113,800 in mission 6 (111): the same
# numbers before and after the integration (the memory was already free at the world's load). The checks
# are measured minus 2 KB (134 / 128 / 109): a guard on this work, not the game's floor; the a1200 has 1.2 MB. The game's floors, 96 KB
# (memory.agk, the world 2 scenarios) and 64 KB (chipwinuae), are untouched. World 1 now plays with 151 KB (tests/splashfree.agk guards 149).
wait-serial "AGK t0" 1000
key 0x63
key 0x28
wait 5
key 0x11
wait 5
key 0x04
wait-serial "AGK world 2 loaded" 700
wait 60
key 0x63
key 0x28
wait 5
key 0x11
wait 5
key 0x05
wait-serial "AGK mission set=5" 400
wait 60
key 0x63
key 0x28
wait 5
key 0x11
wait 5
key 0x06
wait-serial "AGK mission set=6" 400
wait 120
key 0x63
key 0x28
wait 5
key 0x11
wait 5
key 0x05
wait-serial "AGK mission set=5" 400
wait 60
expect-serial "AGK w2 chipfree=(13[4-9]|1[4-9][0-9]|[2-9][0-9][0-9]|[0-9]{4})\b[\s\S]*AGK mission set=5 w2 chipfree=(12[89]|1[3-9][0-9]|[2-9][0-9][0-9]|[0-9]{4})\b[\s\S]*AGK mission set=6 w2 chipfree=(109|11[0-9]|1[2-9][0-9]|[2-9][0-9][0-9]|[0-9]{4})\b[\s\S]*AGK mission set=5 w2 chipfree=(12[89]|1[3-9][0-9]|[2-9][0-9][0-9]|[0-9]{4})\b"
expect-no-serial "AGK ERR|missing"
expect-no-dropped-frames
expect-min-chip-free 96
